[38;5;231m●[39m Verified the captures myself. Here's what we actually have — and one important gap.

  [1mConfirmed: idle and typed[0m

  Codex's TUI is structurally different from Claude's, so none of agendo's existing pane heuristics will transfer:

  ┌──────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │              │                Claude Code                 │                             Codex                              │
  ├──────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ prompt glyph │ [38;5;153m❯[39m                                          │ [38;5;153m›[39m (U+203A, bold)                                               │
  ├──────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ input box    │ between the last two [38;5;153m─{20,}[39m rules          │ [1mno rules at all[0m — a background-color band, [38;5;153m\x1b[48;2;56;64;67m[39m │
  ├──────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ status       │ inferred ([38;5;153mesc to interrupt[39m, token counter) │ an explicit footer word: [38;5;153mReady[39m                                 │
  └──────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  The idle footer, verbatim:

  gpt-5.6-sol high · ~/git/voice-orchestrator · Ready · Approve for me · weekly 99% left

  [38;5;153mReady[39m sits in its own color slot ([38;5;153m38;2;200;169;238[39m), separated by [38;5;153m·[39m.

  [1mThe placeholder trap is real, and it's the same one you already fixed for Claude in [38;5;153m0eea318[39m.[0m The idle box isn't empty — it shows a greyed example prompt:

  idle:   ␛[1m›␛[0m␛[48;2;56;64;67m ␛[2mSummarize recent commits␛[0m     cursor 2,91
  typed:  ␛[1m›␛[0m␛[48;2;56;64;67m Briefly, in one sentence: what…      cursor 57,91

  Plain text alone can't tell those apart — "Summarize recent commits" reads exactly like a real draft. Two signals do: the placeholder is wrapped in [38;5;153m␛[2m[39m (dim) and the caret sits at column 2. That's the same faint-vs-real discrimination [38;5;153minputRealText[39m
  already implements, so it should port.

  [1mNot captured: the busy state[0m

  The one-sentence question came back in under 1.5 s, so all 20 post-Enter frames landed after completion — every one already reading [38;5;153mReady[39m. The two frames that hash differently differ only because [1mthe pane was resized 383→255 columns mid-run[0m, reflowing
  the text; it isn't a busy indicator. So we have [1mzero[0m evidence of what codex shows mid-turn: no spinner frame, no interrupt hint, no elapsed timer. I'd rather say that plainly than guess at a string to match on.

  The agent's attempt at a slower follow-up was blocked by the sandbox classifier, so it couldn't retry.

